Name: noVNC
URL: https://github.com/novnc/noVNC
Version: 1.7.0
Revision: 63107bd06d9e1f6136ff21aeda8cd62cbf0d433e
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: MPL-2.0, MIT, BSD-3-Clause
License File: /brave/third_party/novnc/LICENSE.txt
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes
CPEPrefix: unknown

Description:
The noVNC core RFB library (core/) and its zlib dependency (vendor/pako/),
used by chrome://ko-machines to show remote desktops in a tab. The page hands
RFB a WebSocket-like channel backed by the KOMachineBridge Mojo data pipes, so
no websockify server is involved.

Apple Remote Desktop authentication (security type 30, used by macOS Screen
Sharing) is supported in this version (core/rfb.js, _negotiateARDAuth).

Local Modifications:
- Only core/, vendor/pako/, AUTHORS, LICENSE.txt and the referenced license
  texts in docs/ are vendored; app/, tests/ and utils/ are not.
- Added core/rfb.d.ts: TypeScript declarations for the parts of the RFB API
  K-O uses. The JavaScript is unmodified.

To update: copy core/ and vendor/pako/ from the new tag, review the diff of
core/websock.js (raw channel contract) and core/rfb.js (security types), and
update Version and Revision.
